39 FINLAYSON STREET, ROSANNA • DATE PUBLISHED: 30 SEP 2026
Architectural, renovated and built to last

Set on approximately 625m² with a prized northeast-facing courtyard aspect, this is the kind of family home that offers something increasingly hard to find; genuine space, established gardens and an architect-designed layout that still works beautifully decades later.

Four bedrooms, two living zones, multiple outdoor areas and a deep connection to the garden give the home immediate family appeal, while its Merchant Builders pedigree, generous landholding and walkable Rosanna location add a sense of lasting substance.

Designed by acclaimed architect Graeme Gunn AM and built in 1971, the home was created around light, landscape and the way people actually live. Those principles remain obvious today, enhanced by thoughtful renovations and upgrades completed across 30 years of ownership.

At the heart of the home, the renovated kitchen is fitted with premium AEG appliances including a combi steam oven, combi microwave oven, induction cooktop and integrated dishwasher, alongside a quality Qasair rangehood, and overlooks the open-plan dining and living area. A fireplace adds warmth, while doors open directly to the covered north-facing pergola and entertaining area, creating an easy connection between indoor living and long lunches, family gatherings and time spent outdoors.

A separate family room gives the floorplan another layer, complete with extensive built-in storage, a desk and access to its own private deck. Whether used as a second lounge, work zone or retreat, it adds valuable separation without disconnecting from the rest of the home.

The main bedroom sits privately near the entry with built-in robes, an ensuite and direct rear garden access. Three further bedrooms include a particularly spacious rear bedroom with extensive shelving, while the renovated central bathroom features a standalone bath and underfloor heating.

Outside, the garden brings real depth to the property. A pond and reticulated creek at the front, and at the rear, raised vegetable beds, herbs and fruit trees including plum, pear, pomegranate, nectarine, fig, lime, mandarin and mulberry. There is a powered workshop, rainwater tank and access to the rear from both sides.

A charming, purpose-built chicken [GB1.1]coop and secure run add a touch of country character with the flexibility to suit chickens, small pets or even become an outdoor catio.

The home has been carefully evolved over time, with renovations to the kitchen, laundry and bathrooms, updated flooring, plumbing improvements, solar panels, solar hot water, landscaping and recent painting among the works completed. Heating and cooling are provided throughout via split systems, gas heating, ceiling fans and attention to crossflow air movement in summer.

The location adds another layer of appeal. Rosanna Station, local shops, supermarket and two primary schools are all around 600 metres away, while extensive parkland and play spaces begin approximately 200 metres from home. Macleod College is around two kilometres away via surrounding parkland.

For buyers looking beyond the next few years, the combination of a substantial block, four-bedroom accommodation, architectural pedigree and a tightly connected Rosanna setting gives this home an appeal that extends well beyond first impressions.


